   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Numbers from 11 to 20",
     "texto": [
      "**Unsprezece** means «eleven» and **douăzeci** means «twenty». Between 11 and 19, **ani** goes directly after the number; with **douăzeci**, we say **douăzeci de ani**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Plurals of family words",
     "texto": [
      "Some plurals change quite a lot: **frate → frați**, **soră → surori**, **copil → copii**. With the definite article, the article is added at the end: **frații**, **surorile**, **copiii**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Plural possessives",
     "texto": [
      "The possessive comes after the noun: **frații mei** («my brothers»), **surorile mele** («my sisters»). «Mei» goes with masculine plural nouns and «mele» with feminine plural nouns."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
